{
  "$comment": "Stage-2 semantic-erasure-closure measurements (REL-VIEW-ALGEBRA-01). A closure separates ONE semantic intervention (the `carrier`, a single discriminator substitution) from the deterministic representational normalization it induces, because a tagged union is a dependent sum rather than a product of independently present coordinates: `toGrain` exists only under aggregate-to-grain, `keep` only under project. NORMALIZATION IS AN OPERATION, NOT A COORDINATE — `forget-branch-field` deletes a branch-conditional field, which destroys every semantic coordinate carried inside it, and that FOOTPRINT is what the closure depends on. Naming the dependency after the handle that implemented the deletion under-reported it: `toGrain` costs four coordinates, not one, and `join.cardinality` costs seven. It is a WITNESS CLASSIFICATION, never a sixth subtraction disposition — the code-owned ledger vocabulary is unchanged and a `provisional` closure leaves its candidate `unresolved`. Nothing here writes to witnesses.json and no coordinate named here reaches primitiveRatified; closure.ts asserts that directly. This file is AUTHORED, not regenerated: `checkClosures` re-derives operations and footprints from the branch signatures and the census, and fails when a hand edit moves either.",
